                <div class="case-study-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">
                            02 — Orinoco-inspired Littoral Zone
                        </p>

                        <h2>
                            Where land<br />
                            meets water.
                        </h2>
                    </div>

                    <p class="case-study-intro">
                        A curated interpretation of the shallow margins of the
                        Orinoco basin, where land, water and vegetation meet.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="case-study-body">
                    <div class="case-study-story">
                        <p>
                            Long-leaved aquatic plants, emergent growth, leaf
                            litter, wood and a diverse community of small
                            organisms recreate the layered structure and quiet
                            complexity of a natural littoral zone — adapted into
                            a living ecosystem for the home.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            The Nannostomus occupy the open, upper layers of the
                            aquarium, moving calmly between the vegetation in
                            loose groups. Their characteristic hovering posture
                            and subtle social interactions create a constantly
                            shifting presence in the water column.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Closer to the substrate, Apistogramma viejita occupy
                            a very different ecological niche. They are
                            territorial, inquisitive and closely associated with
                            the structure of the littoral zone.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Together, the two species inhabit different layers
                            of the ecosystem: Nannostomus in the open water
                            above, and Apistogramma among the leaf litter and
                            structure below.
                        </p>
                    </div>

